// Targets a touched ALLY, not the caster -- `SelfBuff` always lands its
// effect on the caster (`entity: data.entity` in
// common/src/states/self_buff.rs), never a touched ally, so this uses
// `BasicMelee` with the engine's established touch-ally heal pattern (see
// spare_the_dying.ron/weave_transfusion.ron/lesser_restoration.ron): a
// near-inert Stab whose `attack_effect_target: InGroup` redirects the
// effect onto whoever is struck instead of dealing damage.
// `AttackSource(Melee)` (not `AnyDamage`) gates the heal for the same reason
// spare_the_dying/weave_transfusion do: `Stab`'s own `AttackDamage` is
// hardcoded to `GroupTarget::OutOfGroup` regardless of `attack_effect_target`
// (common/src/comp/melee.rs), so an `InGroup` hit always accumulates zero
// damage and `AnyDamage` could never fire.
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 35.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        attack_effect: Some((
            Heal(40.0),
            AttackSource(Melee),
        )),
        attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Divine)),
)
